;; clj-kondo configuration for glitter-uikit.
;;
;; jolt.ffi/defcfn defines a var per bound C symbol. clj-kondo cannot see
;; through the macro, so hooks/jolt_ffi.clj rewrites each call into an
;; equivalent `defn` — see that file for why. Without it every
;; objc-msg-send-*/objc-*/cf-* binding in glitter-uikit.ffi, and every call
;; site through the `u` alias in glitter-uikit.appkit / glitter-uikit.widget,
;; is a false "Unresolved symbol"/"Unresolved var".
;;
;; Unlike glitter-gl (whose config.edn excludes an entire verbatim-ported
;; geometry/matrix/shader layer), glitter-uikit has no byte-for-byte-verbatim
;; port needing a blanket exclusion: ffi.clj and widget.clj are ported from
;; glimmer-uikit with documented deviations (see NOTICE.md), not held
;; byte-identical to upstream, so there is no "don't fix, it'd deviate from
;; upstream" case to make here.
;;
;; `:missing-else-branch` is off project-wide: glitter-uikit.widget's
;; markup-validate-element! (and the same guard-clause idiom elsewhere) uses
;; a deliberately else-less `(if-not cond (throw ...))` as an assert, not a
;; two-way branch — the "missing" branch is "fall through to the next form",
;; which is the intended control flow, not an omission.
{:hooks {:analyze-call {jolt.ffi/defcfn hooks.jolt-ffi/defcfn}}
 :linters {:missing-else-branch {:level :off}}}
